        92
       ]
      ]
     },
     {
      "block_label": "aside_text",
      "block_content": "Preprint submitted to Soil Moisture Sensing Letters 12 May 2026",
      "block_bbox": [
       28,
       300,
       64,
       1300
      ],
      "block_id": 1,
      "block_order": null,
      "group_id": 1,
      "global_block_id": 7,
      "global_group_id": 1007,
      "block_polygon_points": [
       [
        28,
        300
       ],
       [
        64,
        300
       ],
       [
        64,
        1300
       ],
       [
        28,
        1300
       ]
      ]
     },
     {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "The sensing fibre was buried at a depth of 0.4 m along a 120 m transect and interrogated every ten minutes for fourteen months. Temperature-corrected strain readings were converted to volumetric water content with a site-specific calibration curve, and the root-mean-square error against ten reference probes was 0.021 m3/m3. Rainfall events produced a sharp rise in apparent water content within thirty minutes at all depths, followed by a slow recession lasting several days. The recession rate differed between the sandy and clayey sections of the transect, which supports a spatially varying drainage coefficient in the site model for forecasting.",
      "block_bbox": [
       100,
       140,
       596,
       640
      ],
      "block_id": 2,
      "block_order": 1,
      "group_id": 2,
      "global_block_id": 8,
      "global_group_id": 1008,
      "block_polygon_points": [
       [
        100,
        140
       ],
       [
        596,
        140
       ],
       [
        596,
        640
       ],
       [
        100,
        640
       ]
      ]
     },
     {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "",
      "block_bbox": [
       628,
       140,
       1124,
       640
      ],
      "block_id": 3,
      "block_order": 2,
      "group_id": 3,
      "global_block_id": 9,
      "global_group_id": 1009,
      "block_polygon_points": [
       [
        628,
        140
       ],
       [
        1124,
        140
       ],
       [
        1124,
        640
       ],
       [
        628,
        640
       ]
      ]
     },
     {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "The effective permittivity $\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{eff}}$ of the soil follows a power-law mixing rule, and the calibrated exponent $\\beta$ was close to 0.5 at every site. This agrees with the refractive model that is commonly used for dielectric mixtures, although the fit degrades above 40% saturation.",
      "block_bbox": [
       100,
       700,
       596,
       980
      ],
      "block_id": 4,
      "block_order": 3,
      "group_id": 4,
      "global_block_id": 10,
      "global_group_id": 1010,
      "block_polygon_points": [
       [
        100,
        700
       ],
       [
        596,
        700
       ],
       [
        596,
        980
       ],
       [
        100,
        980
       ]
      ]
     },
     {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "Writing $\\theta_{v}$ for the volumetric content and $\\theta_{s}$ for the saturated value, the relative saturation is their ratio. All values are expressed in m3/m3 throughout, and the detector also marked that unit string as a formula, so three boxes lie inside this block for only two formulas in the recognised text.",
      "block_bbox": [
       628,
       700,
       1124,
       980
      ],
      "block_id": 5,
      "block_order": 4,
      "group_id": 5,
      "global_block_id": 11,
      "global_group_id": 1011,
      "block_polygon_points": [
       [
        628,
        700
       ],
       [
        1124,
        700
       ],
       [
        1124,
        980
       ],
       [
        628,
        980
       ]
      ]
     },
     {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "Temperature compensation was applied with a second, strain-free fibre laid next to the sensing fibre, so that thermal drift and strain could be separated without assuming a fixed thermal coefficient.",
      "block_bbox": [
       100,
       1030,
       596,
       1230
      ],
      "block_id": 6,
      "block_order": 5,
      "group_id": 6,
      "global_block_id": 12,
      "global_group_id": 1012,
      "block_polygon_points": [
       [
        100,
        1030
       ],
       [
        596,
        1030
       ],
       [
        596,
        1230
       ],
       [
        100,
        1230
       ]
      ]
     },
     {
      "block_label": "text",
      "block_content": "Drift in the interrogator itself was below 0.8 microstrain over the whole campaign, which is negligible compared with the signal produced by a typical rainfall event.",
      "block_bbox": [
       100,
       1190,
       596,
       1390
      ],
      "block_id": 7,
      "block_order": 6,
      "group_id": 7,
      "global_block_id": 13,
